    <briefdescription>
<para>Promotes interesting constant into global variables. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The motivating example is: static const <ref refid="classuint16__t" kindref="compound">uint16_t</ref> TableA[32] = { 41944, 40330, 38837, 37450, 36158, 34953, 33826, 32768, 31776, 30841, 29960, 29128, 28340, 27595, 26887, 26215, 25576, 24967, 24386, 23832, 23302, 22796, 22311, 21846, 21400, 20972, 20561, 20165, 19785, 19419, 19066, 18725, };</para>
<para>uint8x16x4_t LoadStatic(void) { uint8x16x4_t ret; ret.val[0] = vld1q_u16(TableA + 0); ret.val[1] = vld1q_u16(TableA + 8); ret.val[2] = vld1q_u16(TableA + 16); ret.val[3] = vld1q_u16(TableA + 24); return ret; }</para>
<para>The constants in this example are folded into the uses. Thus, 4 different constants are created.</para>
<para>As their type is vector the cheapest way to create them is to load them for the memory.</para>
<para>Therefore the final assembly final has 4 different loads. With this pass enabled, only one load is issued for the constants. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
